===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*leykʷ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|lone}}, {{m|enm|lane}}, from {{der|en|non|lán}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*laihną}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*leykʷ-||to leave (over)}}.

Cognate with {{cog|is|lán}}, {{cog|sv|lån}}, {{cog|da|lån}}, {{cog|de|Lehen||fief}}, {{cog|nl|leen||fief}}, {{cog|fy|lien}}, {{cog|frr|leen||fief; loan; office}}, {{cog|sco|lane}}, {{m|sco|lain}}, {{m|sco|len}}, {{cog|ang|lǣn}}. More at {{m|en|lend}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|law|banking|finance}} An act or instance of [[lend]]ing, an act or instance of [[grant]]ing something for [[temporary]] use.
#: {{syn|en|loaning|lending}}
#: {{ux|en|Because of the '''loan''' that John made to me, I was able to pay my tuition for the upcoming semester.}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''loan''' secured against your own house}}
# {{senseid|en|Q189539}}{{lb|en|law|banking|finance}} A sum of [[money]] or other [[property]] that a natural or legal person [[borrow]]s from another with the condition that it be returned or repaid over time or at a later date (sometimes with [[interest]]).
#: {{syn|en|principal}}
#: {{ux|en|All '''loans''' from the library, whether books or audio material, must be returned within two weeks.}}
#: {{ux|en|He got a '''loan''' of five thousand pounds.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=2|passage=''That'' the young Mr. Churchills liked—but they did not like him coming round of an evening and drinking weak whisky-and-water while he held forth on railway debentures and corporation '''loans'''. Mr. Barrett, however, by fawning and flattery, seemed to be able to make not only Mrs. Churchill but everyone else do what he desired.}}
# The contract and array of legal or ethical obligations surrounding a loan.
#: {{ux|en|He made a payment on his '''loan'''.}}
# The permission to [[borrow]] any item.
#: {{ux|en|Thank you for the '''loan''' of your lawn mower.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/cgk25218261o|date=13 March 2026|work=w:BBC|title=Eustace 'confident' in O'Donnell after Vickers blow|passage=And while Thompson has yet to make a first-team appearance for Derby, he got experience playing for Braintree Town on '''loan''' in the National League earlier this season.<br>Eustace also said that there would be no option to bring in an emergency '''loan''' cover for as long as O'Donnell remains fit.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260314183221/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/cgk25218261o|archivedate=14 March 2026}}

